# UI styling (Nuxt UI + Tailwind)

The `theme/` folder is **not** a design reference. Do not port markup, classes, or layout from theme HTML templates.

## Allowed

- Nuxt UI components (`UButton`, `UCard`, `UFooter`, …)
- Component `:ui` prop for slot/variant overrides (see `.nuxt/ui/<component>.ts` for slot names)
- Standard Tailwind CSS utility classes on elements
- Semantic Nuxt UI colors (`text-default`, `bg-elevated`, `border-muted`, …)

## Not allowed

- Copying structure or styles from `theme/`
- Custom CSS files or `<style>` blocks unless the user explicitly asks
- Raw Tailwind palette colors when a semantic token exists (`text-gray-500` → prefer `text-muted`)
- Inline styles or one-off design tokens outside Nuxt UI / Tailwind defaults

## Workflow

1. Compose with Nuxt UI primitives first.
2. Tune appearance with `:ui` and Tailwind classes.
3. Match brand/layout intent from product context, not from theme files.
